   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the Pilgrim Wesleyan Church to retroactively apply for a real property tax exemption for certain property in the town of Ramapo, county of Rockland",
    "basePrintNo": "S7046",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7046-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7046\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize the Pilgrim Wesleyan Church to retroactively apply\nfor a real property tax exemption for certain property in the town of\nRamapo, county of Rockland\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo authorize the town of Ramapo to accept an application for real\nproperty tax exemption from the Pilgrim Wesleyan Church in the village\nof Spring Valley, town of Ramapo.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 authorizes the town of Ramapo, county of Rockland, to accept\nthe Pilgrim Wesleyan Church an application or renewal application for\nexemption from real property taxes. Section 2 provides for an\nimmediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nPilgrim Wesleyan Church is a not-for-profit organization that would be\nentitled to such an exemption if the organization filled an\napplication or renewal application for the exemption by the\nappropriate taxable status date.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2010 - New Bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
